{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his witty and fast-paced dialogue. the film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and CEO of facebook, and andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, zuckerberg's friend and business partner.\n\nthe movie begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, who is trying to get into one of the school's exclusive final clubs. after being rejected, zuckerberg creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also gets zuckerberg into trouble with the university.\n\nlater, zuckerberg is approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss, who ask him to help them create a social networking site for harvard students. zuckerberg agrees, but eventually drops the project and instead creates his own site, which he calls thefacebook. the site quickly gains popularity, and zuckerberg becomes a celebrity on campus.\n\nas the site grows, zuckerberg brings in eduardo saverin, his friend and business partner, to help him manage the site's finances. however, the two friends eventually have a falling out, and saverin is pushed out of the company. the movie also explores the relationship between zuckerberg and his girlfriend, erica albright, who is played by rooney mara.\n\none of the strengths of the movie is its dialogue, which is clever and engaging. the film's script is full of witty one-liners and clever put-downs, which add to the movie's humor and charm. the film's cast is also excellent, with eisenberg and garfield delivering standout performances.\n\nthe movie's direction is also noteworthy, with fincher using a combination of close-ups and wide shots to create a sense of intimacy and grandeur. the film's score, which was composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also excellent, and adds to the movie's tense and emotional moments.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-crafted and engaging film that explores the complexities of friendship, ambition, and success. the movie's themes are timeless, and its story is both fascinating and thought-provoking. while the film may not be entirely accurate, it is a compelling and entertaining portrayal of the founding of facebook and the people behind it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0032289293594658375}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.04858766868710518}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.00862350407987833}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.16893017292022705}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.000523430178873241}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.4065585434436798}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.005244189407676458}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.03827033191919327}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.0001394651480950415}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.3132617473602295}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.8778288960456848}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.26574259996414185}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -2.753696753643453e-05}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0011300613405182958}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -5.483612312673358e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0007359656738117337}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -5.364403477869928e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.27680420875549316}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.05800475925207138}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token":